Caveat (own finding, not a defect): this package's flutter_test_config.dart
disables platform goldens and, like all `flutter test` runs without an
explicit loadAppFonts() call, renders with the deterministic test/block font,
not the real PublicSans/Inter faces -- so the SPECIFIC price strings used
here ('12.00 د.إ' etc.) trip `scaled=true` under the block font's wider glyph
metrics even though the SAME strings measured ~68px (well under the real
85px threshold) when measured live on-device via the app's own
_naturalWidth()/TextPainter with the real fonts loaded (see
ac1-vm-service-measurements.log §1). The test's PASS is still meaningful --
it exercises the real Column branch's real code and asserts real,
non-vacuous width/order invariants -- but its specific price string should
not be read as "reachable with these exact digits in production"; the actual
real-font reachability threshold and real-catalog ceiling are established
separately in ac1-vm-service-measurements.log.
